{"case_id":"C026","gap_exists":false,"gap_type":[],"confidence":99,"affected_functions":[],"reason":"The change only rewrites the compiler-attribute macro from variadic `JANSSON_ATTRS(...)` to single-argument `JANSSON_ATTRS(x)` and parenthesizes every attribute argument. It changes declaration annotations such as `warn_unused_result` and `format(printf, ...)`, but introduces no runtime entry point, protocol, state, configuration, input semantics, or attack surface for fuzzing. H0 continues to exercise `json_loadb`, `json_dumps`, and `json_dump_callback`; the other edited declarations have no changed executable behavior visible in the supplied case.","evidence":["`src/jansson.h` changes `#define JANSSON_ATTRS(...) __attribute__((__VA_ARGS__))` to `#define JANSSON_ATTRS(x) __attribute__(x)`.","All corresponding edits only replace forms such as `JANSSON_ATTRS(warn_unused_result)` with `JANSSON_ATTRS((warn_unused_result))`.","The multi-attribute declarations `json_sprintf` and `json_vsprintf` merely wrap `warn_unused_result, format(printf, ...)` in an additional pair of parentheses.","No function body, flag value, callback contract, data structure, or control flow is changed in `src/hashtable.h`, `src/jansson.h`, `src/jansson_private.h`, or `src/strbuffer.h`.","H0 invokes the unchanged APIs `json_loadb`, `json_dumps`, and `json_dump_callback` with fuzz-derived flags and payload data."],"recommended_action":"Do not add a fuzz target for this change; validate the attribute-macro rewrite through compiler/build coverage instead."}
